                    {
                        "sense_id": "347f424a-7cb7-3bd3-bfe1-43ee10abde6f",
                        "entry_id": "1587e07f-de9a-3d82-a2fb-1b2889b61689",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Niveau de l'emploi en dessus du potentiel d’une personne, d’une organisation en particulier ou d'une économie en général."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Économie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7288b3e3-423f-4ee8-b06b-e8c36a32acc1",
                                "sense_id": "347f424a-7cb7-3bd3-bfe1-43ee10abde6f",
                                "text": "Lors d'une audition devant la commission de la Défense de l'Assemblée nationale, le général Jean-Pierre Kelche, chef d'état-major des armées, constatait récemment que les unités du COS, “largement engagées notamment dans les Balkans”, étaient “pratiquement en suremploi”."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5a39eb83-c9e7-41f6-a269-5482cb8bb786",
                        "source_entry_id": "1587e07f-de9a-3d82-a2fb-1b2889b61689",
                        "source_sense_id": "347f424a-7cb7-3bd3-bfe1-43ee10abde6f",
                        "target_lang_word": "overemployment",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "overemployment",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "340a3189-8e3c-37f2-bd8d-cf37fe63f257",
                                        "entry_id": "480178be-1902-35ab-9bff-d7382518bc18",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being overemployed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95d53bc4-f0a0-4c77-940b-ada99e32037c",
                                                "sense_id": "340a3189-8e3c-37f2-bd8d-cf37fe63f257",
                                                "text": "People who remain overemployed tolerate longer hours because they either expect their overemployment to be brief (such as temporary care-giving), or figure that part-time or reduced hours status involves too large a sacrifice in terms of benefit coverage or job status."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb70b03f-77ca-4c91-9f10-c0e45a4c6f9b",
                                                "sense_id": "340a3189-8e3c-37f2-bd8d-cf37fe63f257",
                                                "text": "In sum, survey estimates of overemployment may be biased downward if a survey provokes certain implicit assumptions about the current income foregone, and the amount and dimensions of hours reduced and type of gains realized in time off."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5395f48-6b10-429e-9d00-477c305cb205",
                                                "sense_id": "340a3189-8e3c-37f2-bd8d-cf37fe63f257",
                                                "text": "Labor-leisure models portray overemployment as an individual labor-market phenomenon, but it can also be viewed from a macroeconomic perspective."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
